.TH DOCUBACK 1 2026-09-13 "DocuBrowse 1.5.2" "DocuBrowse Manual"
.SH NAME
docuback \- back up and restore DocuBrowse runtime data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docuback \-\-backup
.RI [ "\-\-db PATH" ]
.RI [ "\-\-backup\-dir PATH" ]
.br
.B docuback \-\-restore
.RI [ "\-\-db PATH" ]
.RI [ "\-\-backup\-dir PATH" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docuback
backs up and restores the runtime data of a DocuBrowse installation \(em the
SQLite database and its associated files \(em so an index can be preserved
across reinstalls or moved between machines.
.P
Exactly one of
.B \-\-backup
or
.B \-\-restore
must be given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-backup
Create a backup of the current runtime data.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Restore runtime data from a previous backup.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " PATH"
Operate on the SQLite database at
.IR PATH ,
overriding the configured
.IR db_path .
.TP
.BI \-\-backup\-dir " PATH"
Read or write backups in
.IR PATH
instead of the default backup directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B docuback
exits 0 on success and non-zero on error, for example when a backup file is
missing or the destination is not writable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.docubrowser/
Per-user runtime data directory backed up and restored by this tool.
.SH EXAMPLES
Back up the current index:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
docuback \-\-backup
.EE
.in
.P
Restore from a specific backup directory:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
docuback \-\-restore \-\-backup\-dir /media/usb/docubrowse\-backups
.EE
.in
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docubrowser (1),
.BR docubrowse.config (5)
